19:
@G[Swapping wrestler positions]@D
　　Select the wrestler to move with $a$b
　　and press $0, then select the place
　　to move to the same way to swap
　　the 2 positions.

@G[Switching MAN and CPU]@D
　　Switch with $c$d.
　　@YAll Players@D makes everyone a
　　@BMAN@D controlled by a player, and
　　@YAll CPU@D makes everyone a @BCPU@D
　　controlled by the computer.

20:
@G[Swapping wrestler positions]@D
　　Select the wrestler to move with $a$b
　　and press $0, then select the place
　　to move to the same way to swap
　　the 2 positions.
　　If the bracket is split left and
　　right, switch sides with $2$3.

@G[Switching MAN and CPU]@D
　　Switch with $c$d.
　　@YAll Players@D makes everyone a
　　@BMAN@D controlled by a player, and
　　@YAll CPU@D makes everyone a @BCPU@D
　　controlled by the computer.

38:
Move wrestlers made in Edit Mode
from the cartridge to the
@BController Pak@D, or from the
@BController Pak@D to the cart.

@G(How to)@D
　　Select the wrestler to move with $f
　　and press $0. Then select where to
　　move to the same way and press $0
　　to swap them.
@Y(Note)@D
　　It is @Rnot final@D until you select
　　@BConfirm@D at the very bottom of the
　　screen.

6:
You can create your own original Wrestler here.
A created Wrestler can participate in any match
freely.

Also, you can save created Wrestlers to a
@BController Pak@D and trade them with friends.

@Y(Note)@D
　　If a Wrestler was originally included in the
　　game (not a created Wrestler), only their
　　@GProfile @Dand @GAppearance @Dcan be edited.
